WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:03.326
A useful way to read requirements is to look for
different kinds

00:00:03.353 --> 00:00:09.876
of language Nouns often suggest candidate entities
Descriptive

00:00:09.903 --> 00:00:16.139
facts often become attributes Verbs often reveal
relationships Words

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:20.087
such as must may only and at least often reveal
constraints or

00:00:20.113 --> 00:00:26.792
optionality For example patient and provider are
nouns Birth

00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:31.186
date is a descriptive fact about a patient A patient
books an

00:00:31.213 --> 00:00:36.897
appointment describes a relationship Every
appointment must have one provider describes

00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:42.446
a required relationship Do not start by typing
CREATE TABLE

00:00:44.163 --> 00:00:48.823
Start by writing the business meaning in plain
language Once the meaning

00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:53.034
is clear translating it into a relational structure
becomes much easier
